From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:25:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 181/342] meson_vdec, meson_decoder: streams whose picture size
 changes

H.264: the driver set up the frames for a new size as soon as the firmware
asked, while frames of the old size were still queued, so GET_FRAME gave
them the new size (and the firmware took frames the reader still held as
free). Now every setup waits until the reader has taken and given back all
frames; GET_FRAME tells a reader that holds frames to give them back
(MESON_VDEC_FRAME_GIVE_BACK).

HEVC: frames were set up only for a session's first picture, so a new
size went on with the old one. Now a picture of another size, CTB size or
bit depth hands out the pictures so far, waits for all frames back and
sets up new ones.

meson_decoder gives back what it holds when asked (as before a seek), shows
frames in place only when they have the negotiated size, and scales others
to fit in it, black around them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
